# Architecture

Two layers, from the Flutter app-architecture guide. No domain layer and no use cases.

| Piece | Role |
| --- | --- |
| View | `StatelessWidget` that renders cubit state |
| View model | One `Cubit` per screen |
| Repository | Only type a cubit calls for I/O |
| Service | API class used only by its repository |

Dependency direction: view → cubit → repository → service → `Dio`.

```
lib/
  main.dart                 # bind Flutter, runApp
  app/                      # MaterialApp.router, GoRouter, theme
  core/error/failure.dart   # sealed Failure
  core/error/result.dart    # sealed Result<T>
  core/network/             # shared Dio
  core/storage/             # secure token storage
  features/<feature>/data/dto/
  features/<feature>/data/repositories/
  features/<feature>/data/  # API services
  features/<feature>/presentation/<screen>/
```

A page owns `BlocProvider`. The view owns `BlocBuilder` / `BlocListener`. API response models are `*Dto` classes in `data/dto/`. Repositories live in `data/repositories/`. Each screen is its own `presentation/<screen>/` folder with sealed state, Cubit, page, and view.
